# API — Security Rules

## JWT — Access + Refresh Token Pattern

```typescript
// ✅ Access token: short-lived (15 min), in Authorization header
// ✅ Refresh token: long-lived (7 days), stored in Redis + httpOnly cookie

// Issue tokens
const accessToken  = jwt.sign({ userId, email }, env.JWT_SECRET, { expiresIn: '15m' })
const refreshToken = crypto.randomBytes(64).toString('hex')

// Store refresh token in Redis
await redis.setex(`refresh:${userId}:${refreshToken}`, 7 * 24 * 60 * 60, '1')

// Set refresh token in httpOnly cookie — never in response body
res.cookie('refreshToken', refreshToken, {
  httpOnly: true,
  secure: env.NODE_ENV === 'production',
  sameSite: 'strict',
  maxAge: 7 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000,
})

// ❌ Never store refresh token in response body — client JS can read it
res.json({ accessToken, refreshToken })
```

## Authentication Middleware

```typescript
// ✅ Always verify JWT — never trust req.headers without verification
export const authenticate = asyncHandler(async (req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.replace('Bearer ', '')
  if (!token) throw new UnauthorizedError('No token provided')

  const payload = jwt.verify(token, env.JWT_SECRET) as JWTPayload
  req.user = { id: payload.userId, email: payload.email }
  next()
})
```

## Rate Limiting — Redis-Backed

```typescript
// ✅ Rate limit all public endpoints — per IP for auth, per user for authenticated routes
const authRateLimiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,  // 15 minutes
  max: 10,                     // 10 login attempts per 15 min
  keyGenerator: (req) => req.ip,
  message: { success: false, error: { code: 'RATE_LIMITED', message: 'Too many attempts' } },
})

const apiRateLimiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 60 * 1000,         // 1 minute
  max: 120,                    // 120 requests per minute per user
  keyGenerator: (req) => req.user?.id ?? req.ip,
})
```

## Security Headers — Helmet

```typescript
// ✅ Always use helmet — must be the first middleware
app.use(helmet({
  contentSecurityPolicy: {
    directives: {
      defaultSrc:  ["'self'"],
      connectSrc:  ["'self'", env.DASHBOARD_ORIGIN, env.EXTENSION_ORIGIN],
    }
  },
  hsts: { maxAge: 31536000, includeSubDomains: true },
}))
```

## CORS — Whitelist Only

```typescript
// ✅ Whitelist only known origins — never use origin: '*' in production
app.use(cors({
  origin: [env.DASHBOARD_ORIGIN, env.EXTENSION_ORIGIN],
  credentials: true,
  methods: ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'PATCH', 'DELETE'],
}))

// ❌ Never
app.use(cors())           // allows any origin
app.use(cors({ origin: '*' }))
```

## Input — Never Trust User Data

```typescript
// ✅ Validate with Zod before any processing — see api-architecture rule
// ✅ Never use user input directly in MongoDB queries without sanitization
// ✅ Never eval() or new Function() with user input
// ✅ Use parameterized queries — Mongoose handles this automatically

// ❌ Never build filter objects from raw request body
const filter = req.body  // user controls the query
await UserModel.find(filter)

// ✅ Whitelist allowed filter fields explicitly
const { status, modeId } = req.body
await SessionModel.find({ userId: req.user.id, ...(status && { status }), ...(modeId && { modeId }) })
```

## Secrets — Never in Code

```typescript
// ❌ Never hardcode secrets
const JWT_SECRET = 'my-secret-key'
const GROQ_KEY = 'gsk_abc123'

// ✅ Always from validated env
const JWT_SECRET = env.JWT_SECRET
const GROQ_KEY = env.GROQ_API_KEY
```
